      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Opioids are an effective treatment for chronic non-malignant pain (CNP). Long-term use risks and side effects such as opioid-induced androgen deficiency (OPIAD) exist. This could be measured by saliva testosterone (Sal-T)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "To evaluate OPIAD in long-term opioid use in CNP patients."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "A cross-sectional study included CNP male outpatients under opioid treatment. Total-Testosterone (Total-T), Free-Testosterone (Free-T), Bio-Testosterone (Bio-T) and Sal-T were measured. Correlations were calculated by Spearman's rho (SPSS 20)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "From 2012 to 2014, 134 from 249 (54%) consecutive male outpatients reported erectile dysfunction (ED), 37% of them related to opioids and 19% evidenced OPIAD. A total of 120 subjects (94 cases and 26 matched-controls) were included. A significantly lower luteinizing hormone, Total-T and Free-T were found, as well as, a significant correlation between Sal-T and Total-T (r\u2009=\u20090.234, p\u2009=\u20090.039), Bio-T (r\u2009=\u20090.241, p\u2009=\u20090.039), IIEF (r\u2009=\u20090.363, p\u2009=\u20090.003) and HAD-anxiety (r =\u2009-0.414, p\u2009=\u20090.012) in OPIAD patients. Sal-T levels were significantly lower in patients with severe-moderate ED versus mild ED (p\u2009=\u20090.045) and in patients with severe ED versus moderate-mild ED (p\u2009=\u20090.036)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "These data demonstrate the high prevalence of ED in long-term use of opioids, part of this is associated to OPIAD, which can be tested by Sal-T as a non-invasive approach."
        }
      ]},
